Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["InfraCircle", "ObjectName",
 CellID->1224892054,ExpressionUUID->"8393d601-4014-44ba-afc9-60862df940ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"3bb9bdc4-f916-49af-85a2-847a2c0b2dce"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraCircle"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraCircle", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "efa3f285-e7e5-41d0-b954-369f6ec56ab6"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "is the family of circles around ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 " at radius ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 ". It is a symbolic object; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraMeasurement"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMeasurement", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "2279379b-35ab-4cd3-a78c-b470b01ac3e6"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["RandomInfraCircle"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/RandomInfraCircle", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "c0593bed-72f0-4ee3-99b5-ff48f0d2f842"],
 " evaluate it on a graph.",
 "\n",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"c4b18a4d-201f-4a6d-87a3-a88137434974"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraCircle"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraCircle", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["r", "TI"], ",", " ", 
      StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a676e24f-c0ae-4975-baa5-23e74a377293"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "is the family in the band ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " \[LessEqual] ",
 StyleBox["d(c, v)", "TI"],
 " \[LessEqual] ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 "; a scalar ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " means ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", "r"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0007fac5-92a9-42b8-b2b3-21c390c586a8"],
 ".",
 "\n",
 "The same expression inside an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraScene"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraScene", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "b58ec17e-3ec8-451d-9e3a-866997e1e0b2"],
 " is the circle construction token."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"0cc9172e-d178-4486-836b-1b3af5f13ff8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Definition: a circle of the band ",
 StyleBox["W", "TI"],
 " around ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 " is a shortest cycle of the subgraph induced on ",
 StyleBox["W", "TI"],
 " whose removal leaves ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 " in a component that reaches no further than the band."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"2b9655c5-fb0f-4ea9-a457-ef93ffd2954b"],

Cell["\<\
The second argument is always a radius or a band, never a point, so a vertex \
label that is an integer or a pair cannot be mistaken for one. There are no \
options.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d553c977-95cf-4ca4-bd20-74e739c92eb5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Euclid's third postulate describes a circle with any centre and distance: \
the circle is named by its radius. The circle through a point ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " is drawn by a compass opened to ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 ", an arc that closes: it is the closed arc ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraArc"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraArc", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", " ", 
      StyleBox["p", "TI"]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1299eb97-b3e6-4700-a27d-2c2c693a3773"],
 ", the circles of the band of ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " that pass through ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"7ff445ed-5a38-49ee-81c5-f3df0cb8bcce"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["A circle need not exist.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " On a lattice a single distance shell has no two adjacent vertices, so it \
spans no cycle and the family is empty. This is what a sphere of one-vertex \
thickness is on a lattice, not a defect of the definition."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c5860a17-3f07-40f1-987d-f596fd9e9eb8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Widening the radius to a band fixes it, and ",
 StyleBox["the band thickness that suffices tracks the girth of the tiling",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". On the square tiling, girth 4, the band ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"r", " ", "+", " ", "1"}]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c04ca92-0ae5-484a-9b41-66d615a21339"],
 " already carries a circle. On the hexagonal tiling, girth 6, it does not: \
the band has to reach ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"r", " ", "+", " ", "2"}]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c9f5bb0-844f-4c63-a05f-93300fd239ef"],
 ". On the triangular tiling, girth 3, a single shell carries a circle; on an \
irregular mesh it usually does, its vertices being adjacent by accident of \
the mesh."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e8c91f4d-c581-4af0-8deb-115c450fd47e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Its graph \[LongDash] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraMeasurement"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMeasurement", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["circle", "TI"], ",", " ", "\"\<Graph\>\""}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8256e3ae-4ab9-4ee2-8c64-8bb2e85fc42f"],
 " \[LongDash] is a ",
 Cell[BoxData["List"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "40a658ec-ada3-4989-958d-4bd3eb4de48a"],
 " of ",
 StyleBox["atoms",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " of the unrolled band. The band is cut along a radial seam, the band part \
of a shortest path from ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 " to the nearest vertex outside the band, and unrolled: the circles through \
a seam vertex ",
 StyleBox["x", "TI"],
 " are the shortest paths of the cyclic cover of the band from ",
 StyleBox["x", "TI"],
 " to a second copy of ",
 StyleBox["x", "TI"],
 ". An atom is the DAG of those paths for one seam vertex, with the earlier \
seam vertices removed, so every circle lies in exactly one atom, at its first \
seam vertex. Only the atoms of least length are kept: an atom at a seam \
vertex that no shortest circle meets carries longer closed walks only. The \
atom is projected to the vertices of the graph, and its sink is kept as the \
separate vertex ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"3", "/", "2"}]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1997235e-7289-4ce1-9091-9a184e706212"],
 ", a copy of its source ",
 StyleBox["x", "TI"],
 ". So the atom is acyclic, its chains from ",
 StyleBox["x", "TI"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"3", "/", "2"}]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cc756f9d-9b7e-4355-b19d-f7e78e4064f7"],
 " are the circles read as closed walks, and its ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Cardinality\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1324949a-f7ed-49ed-b446-97479ec5d79c"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Length\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f5033e9-d683-49c9-abca-ce627d7a7ffe"],
 " are the chain count and the length of the circle."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"5f5b669e-423b-4d22-a877-d4fae5c12f2d"],

Cell["\<\
The two sides of the seam are told apart by separation alone: two neighbours \
of a seam vertex lie on the same side iff the cycle through them and the cut \
band does not separate. No coordinates enter, and a circle may meet the seam \
any number of times.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"223a6c3d-f486-419a-adbc-398a2833ccdc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The atoms need the cut band to be connected and the two sides to occur on \
the seam. Where the cut band is disconnected, or the seam has one side only, \
the graph is a ",
 Cell[BoxData["List"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5ecf9424-c92f-4038-a404-474d1d253e2d"],
 " of ",
 StyleBox["necklaces",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " instead, cut from the band along the same seam: a DAG with one source ",
 StyleBox["s1", "TI"],
 " and one sink, a copy ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"s1", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"3", "/", "2"}]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e741dce4-519b-49fd-9374-477f73f7cc8a"],
 " of its source, again the cycle family opened at its closing arrow. A \
necklace needs the circle to meet the seam in one run, so it can miss a \
circle."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"120378b4-e9a9-42d5-9322-a5b0f7eae4dc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A member is a chain of the graph read as a cyclic vertex list: the copy of \
the source is dropped and the first vertex is not repeated. The ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Length\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8e36e9b8-ee4e-472d-b051-b63565739fec"],
 " of a circle of ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 " vertices is ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0a132187-165c-4e8e-b582-b9f047f224e7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The search.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["RandomInfraCircle"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/RandomInfraCircle", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["circle", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "165721cf-0bc5-467d-a2e8-e3e38ca4be84"],
 " sweeps the band directly: for ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 " = 3, 4, \[Ellipsis] it takes every cycle of length ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 " of the band (",
 Cell[BoxData["FindCycle"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "40f16989-5bbe-4280-b03a-46add2948631"],
 ") and keeps those whose removal leaves ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 " in a component reaching no further than the band; the first ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 " with a survivor gives the members. It does not read the graph, so it is \
the check on it, and it still answers where nothing lies beyond the band and \
separation is vacuous. Each length is enumerated in full before the filter, \
so the sweep is fast on a band one or two vertices thick and does not finish \
in reasonable time on a wide one, such as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "307f4357-b83e-4085-86f1-283a3f19a2b4"],
 " on the square tiling."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f447513b-c2e3-46ca-a2dc-3f90b369a4e6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every member separates. That the atoms carry every circle exactly once \
needs the winding functional, an invariant of the substrate that is nonzero \
exactly on the separating cycles, and a connected cut band; nothing here \
certifies the first. So ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Faithful\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9d7d976e-926a-4304-9b4b-df3b35b20b24"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Undetermined"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/Undetermined", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "97372665-c772-4f7b-819c-3405248a6669"],
 ", except that it is ",
 Cell[BoxData["False"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8f2b7900-34b7-4189-816c-7c38d7670a1c"],
 " where the cut band is connected and the seam has one side only: there the \
winding functional or the annulus is witnessed to fail."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"33a3dcc3-be1d-4e65-947c-102cbd502d00"],

Cell["Corresponding notions in the classical axiom systems:", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"73a0f348-f1fe-4abb-a5db-6c56839f1e45"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "5ddf2589-8e27-4f6a-9b23-ac43ef5e6204"], Cell["System", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"f6db8909-c96a-44f2-b8fd-24dbd446ee53"],
